ind":"announcement","title":"Irish Sport Manager 0.36.5 - An Improved Match Screen!","summary":"Irish Sport Manager 0.36.5A new match screen for Next Fest, and fixes from a read of the match, the career, the saves, the interface and every line of prose. Notes from 0.36.2: 0.36.3 and 0.36.4 were never released on their own, so everything since is here. The match screenA new layout: a broadcast band across the top in the two counties' colours, with the score, the clock and four figures a side (scores, scores from placed balls, share of the ball, times turned over); a strip under it with what","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-19T01:14:18Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846651706688423","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:03:25Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5050590-1846651706680179","game_id":"steam-5050590","kind":"announcement","title":"Irish Sport Manager 0.36.2","summary":"Irish Sport Manager 0.36.2 Match dayYour first match starts at normal speed (1×). A first-time player's match used to start at TV pace, the slowest setting, by mistake. The speed you pick is still remembered from match to match. Extra time follows each code's rules. In football and hurling any fifteen may start it, so changes at the break before it are free. A player sent off in normal time may be replaced for extra time in football, hurling and ladies' football. Ladies' football and camogie all","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-16T05:52:16Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846651706680179","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:03:25Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5050590-1846018067941581","game_id":"steam-5050590","kind":"announcement","title":"hotfixes","summary":"fixing some scoring bugs I missed.","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-12T16:43:55Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846018067941581","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:03:25Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5050590-1846018067939889","game_id":"steam-5050590","kind":"announcement","title":"Irish Sport Manager 0.36.0: the match field","summary":"Irish Sport Manager 0.36.0: the match field Long balls A long ball that one of the other side is contesting where it comes down, within five metres, breaks at least three times in four, and more when the player contesting it is the better high fielder. It spills two to five metres and the side the match has on the ball next gathers it, whoever is nearest with the best read of a breaking ball. A long ball to a player with nobody near them is caught cleanly every time. Long balls used to stick alm","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-12T03:34:08Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846018067939889","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:03:25Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5050590-1846018067924899","game_id":"steam-5050590","kind":"announcement","title":"Irish Sport Manager 0.35.4","summary":"Irish Sport Manager 0.35.4: kick-outs, frees, cards, marking and the 3/3 rule, and January put right Kick-outs and puck-outs A side keeps its own kick-out about three times in five, as teams did across the 2025 season (59% in the League, 61% in the Sam Maguire, 62% in the Tailteann Cup). It was a straight contest after every score and wide, so both sides seemed to lose almost every kick-out they took. Both sides spread across the field for a kick-out, wide to the wings and out beyond the arc. Th","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-07T03:40:21Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846018067924899","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:03:25Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5050590-1845383656391760","game_id":"steam-5050590","kind":"update","title":"Major Update: Irish Sport Manager 0.35.2","summary":"Irish Sport Manager 0.35.2: January as it is played, the referee, the kick-out from the twenty, and the 2026 football championship The pitch Football kick-outs are taken from the centre of the 20 metre line. The keeper comes out to the ball, every other player clears the ground first, and in men's football both sides line up beyond the 40 metre arc. The ball used to be kicked from the keeper's own spot with four or five players standing around it. Puck-outs in hurling and camogie wait for the tw","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-04T18:00:04Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1845383656391760","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:03:25Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5050590-1845383656379702","game_id":"steam-5050590","kind":"announcement","title":"Irish Sport Manager 0.34.0: every attribute counts","summary":"Irish Sport Manager 0.34.0: every attribute counts, three players marked, and the ball stops flying the pitch The match Every attribute now moves a match. Passing, workrate, tackling and positioning used to count for almost nothing in a result, and handling for far too much. A side better at any one of them now wins more, by about the same amount for each. Kick-outs and puck-outs are three contests: the clean catch, the breaking ball won by the half-lines and midfield who read it and get there, ","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-01T04:05:20Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1845383656379702","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:03:25Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5050590-1844751498229793","game_id":"steam-5050590","kind":"announcement","title":"Irish Sport Manager 0.33.3: the ball at its real speed,","summary":"Irish Sport Manager 0.33.3: the ball at its real speed, the clock that keeps time with it, and each code played its own way The ball The ball flies at its real speed, by code: a struck sliotar at 150 to 180 km/h in hurling and 120 to 140 in camogie, a football kicked at 90 to 110 in the men's game and 75 to 90 in the ladies', a hand-pass at 30 to 50 in every code by its length. It used to be timed by a fixed fraction of a second, which read as ping-pong between players and posts. Nobody outruns ","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-09-27T19:07:39Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1844751498229793","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:03:25Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5050590-1844751498220335","game_id":"steam-5050590","kind":"announcement","title":"Irish Sport Manager 0.33.2: the ball is run with, and thirty men who move on the","summary":"Irish Sport Manager 0.33.2: the ball is run with, and thirty men who move on their own The ball Players run with the ball. The picture only ever passed, marker to marker, and it read as ping-pong. A man in possession now carries it, the ball a stride ahead of him and the ring on him, at his own speed from his pace. In the football codes the wing-backs, wing-forwards and midfield are the ones who run, the 6 and the 11 kick-pass to the inside line, and a carry runs on into the twenty and thirty me","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-09-24T05:40:33Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1844751498220335","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:03:25Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5050590-1844115010490341","game_id":"steam-5050590","kind":"announcement","title":"Irish Sport Manager 0.33.1","summary":"The inbox Continue stops on the day a letter that needs an answer lands: a story, a disciplinary notice inside its reply window, a question from the press. Once, for that letter. Leaving it unanswered is your call, and the button does not trap you on it. Stories that mean it The farm takes him for the fortnight. The summer in Boston is a summer away. A weekend dropped is a weekend in the stand. The squad row says why, the way it does for exams and work. The wedding falls on the eve of your match","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-09-16T23:03:02Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1844115010490341","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:03:25Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5050590-1844115010487872","game_id":"steam-5050590","kind":"announcement","title":"Irish Sport Manager 0.32.1: the first twenty minutes, read again","summary":"Match dayThe commentary walks its lines: no two scores of a kind in a row read the same way. The first ten minutes of a match used to be able to hand the same sentence to the same player twice. The football scoreline carries a note on how it reads, on the scoreboard, the results and the stats: goals, two-pointers, points, so 1-2-12 is nineteen. The openingThe county screen no longer promises a second season's trends on the demo's first day. The scout's letters name the screen they mean: Club cal","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-09-16T01:33:19Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1844115010487872","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:03:25Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5050590-1843481262698548","game_id":"steam-5050590","kind":"announcement","title":"Irish Sport Manager 0.32.0: the match finds its words","summary":"Irish Sport Manager 0.32.0: the match finds its words Match dayThe commentary says a score a dozen ways now, and hurling and camogie have lines of their own. The play by play no longer reads the same sentence thirty times a match. More lines are coming, and the machinery is open: a calls folder beside your stories folder takes your own, in the same plain JSON, and a Workshop pack can carry them. SelectionCover. On the Tactics screen, name up to five men per line, in order. When a starter is out ","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-09-12T23:58:45Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1843481262698548","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:03:25Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5050590-1842846814453689","game_id":"steam-5050590","kind":"update","title":"Small hotfix","summary":"Small hotfix","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-09-07T17:34:19Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1842846814453689","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:03:25Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5050590-1842846814445404","game_id":"steam-5050590","kind":"announcement","title":"Irish Sport Manager 0.31.0: now on Mac","summary":"Irish Sport Manager 0.31.0: now on Mac Mac Irish Sport Manager runs on Mac from this update. The demo and the full game both. Apple silicon and Intel, macOS 10.15 or later, signed and notarised, and Steam installs the right one. It is the same game, the same world, the same saves. A career started on one is not tied to it. It is also new. If something looks wrong on a Mac, the crash reporting is on and the report says where. Say what you saw on the discussion board as well, since a thing that lo","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-09-04T05:27:27Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1842846814445404","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:03:25Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5050590-1842846814440958","game_id":"steam-5050590","kind":"update","title":"Quick Patch","summary":"Irish Sport Manager 0.30.2 A crash hotfix. Nothing else changed, and your career carries on where it was. The exiles could not play a season A career with New York, Warwickshire or Lancashire ended with the game closing, about a month in, with no warning and nothing to be done about it. Those three field one code and not the other. New York play football and no hurling; Warwickshire and Lancashire the other way round, and the same holds in the women's codes. Once a month the backroom writes up w","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-09-02T16:33:45Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1842846814440958","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:03:25Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5050590-1842846814438870","game_id":"steam-5050590","kind":"update","title":"hotfix","summary":"small hotfix","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-09-01T23:58:46Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1842846814438870","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:03:25Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5050590-1842846814438755","game_id":"steam-5050590","kind":"update","title":"Patch Notes: Irish Sport Manager 0.30.0","summary":"Irish Sport Manager 0.30.0This is a big one! Match engineWinning the ball back now leads to a better chance than a set attack does: a defence that has not got players behind the ball concedes more. Overall scoring is unchanged, so the fast break is worth more and the set attack slightly less. A sweeper is half the cover on a fast break, because they are a forward who has not got back yet. Attacking quickly is the counter to the system. Hurling and camogie: the half-forward line now contests the ","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-09-01T23:04:54Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1842846814438755","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:03:25Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5050590-1842212951311715","game_id":"steam-5050590","kind":"update","title":"Patch Notes: Irish Sport Manager 0.29.0","summary":"Patch Notes for Irish Sport Manager (Demo) 0.29.0 Some boneheaded oversight/errors rectified: Rules Camogie: a sideline cut struck over the bar is now worth two points The 40 metre arc now stops short of the sidelines, as it does on a real pitch The 13 metre semi-circle is drawn at the correct size, and on every code Camogie pitches show a 45 metre line, hurling a 65 Calendar The championship finishes in late July instead of late June Two week gaps before the semi-finals and the final The second","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-08-31T23:37:39Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1842212951311715","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:03:25Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5050590-1842212951311282","game_id":"steam-5050590","kind":"update","title":"Patch notes: Irish Sport Manager 0.28.0","summary":"Patch notes: Irish Sport Manager 0.28.0 Gameplay Football scoring raised to about 22 or 23 a team, from 17 Two point efforts up from about 1.6 a game to 2.2 Counties now open in their real 2027 league divisions, football and hurling Hurling and camogie graded 1A and 1B at the top, not 1 and 2 Match screen The 40 metre arc is drawn on the team sheet and the match pitch Hurling and camogie pitches now show their 65 metre line instead of football's 45 Dashed halfway line and the small arc at each 2","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-08-31T19:29:29Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1842212951311282","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:03:25Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5050590-1842212951309566","game_id":"steam-5050590","kind":"announcement","title":"The demo is out now","summary":"The free demo for Irish Sport Manager is live. Download it from the store page above. What's in it A full season, not a slice of one. You take a county and manage it from the league through the championship under the 2026 rules, into the club championship in the autumn, and finish in front of the county board while they decide whether they would have kept you. Eight counties to choose from across the four codes: Football: Mayo, Meath, Waterford Hurling: Clare, Antrim, Sligo Camogie: Cork Ladies'","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-08-31T08:55:49Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1842212951309566","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:03:25Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"}],"analyses":[],"news_status":{"steam-5050590":{"last_attempt_at":"2026-10-26T07:37:57Z","status":"ok","all_sources_checked_at":"2026-10-26T07:37:57Z","error_codes":[]}},"news_last_attempt_at":{"steam-5050590":"2026-10-26T07:37:57Z"},"notices":[],"news_sources":{"5050590":{"last_attempt_at":"2026-10-26T07:37:57Z","last_success_at":"2026-10-26T07:37